Message Queue: A system where producers send messages to a queue and consumers read them asynchronously. Examples: Kafka, RabbitMQ, Pulsar, AWS SQS.
High Throughput: System can process millions of messages per second.
Low Latency: Time between producing a message and consuming it is very small.

Kafka uses log-structured storage for sequential disk writes → very fast.